# Speaking Gym

A single-page tool for practicing speaking out loud — presentations, casual fluency, and interview answers — with a live transcript, filler-word tracking, and a recording you can actually listen back to.

Built as a sibling to [Thinking Gym](../thinking-gym): same visual language, different muscle.

## The three modes

**Presentation** — a 3-minute prompt to give a short talk or pitch on the spot.

**Conversation** — 90-second casual prompts aimed at spoken fluency, not polish.

**Interview** — 2-minute classic behavioral interview questions, answered live.

## How a session works

1. Pick a mode and hit **Start speaking**.
2. Your mic starts recording, and (in supported browsers) your words appear live in a transcript, with filler words — um, uh, like, you know, sort of, basically, actually, and a few others — highlighted as they show up.
3. Live stats track word count, words per minute, and filler count as you talk.
4. Hit **Stop**, and you get a summary: duration, WPM, filler count and rate, plus an audio player to review the actual recording.
5. Save it, and it's added to a session log at the bottom, so you can track sessions over time.

## Running it

Single static HTML file, no build step.

- **Locally:** download `index.html` and open it in a browser.
- **Hosted:** enable GitHub Pages on this repo and it'll be live at `https://<your-username>.github.io/<repo-name>/speaking-gym/`.

Microphone access requires a secure context — this works fine over GitHub Pages (HTTPS) or `localhost`. Some browsers restrict mic access when opening a file directly from disk (`file://`); if the mic prompt never appears, try hosting it rather than double-clicking the file.

## Browser support — please read

- **Live transcript and filler-word tracking require a Chrome-based browser** (Chrome, Edge, Brave, Arc). They rely on the Web Speech API, which Firefox and Safari don't support.
- In unsupported browsers, recording and playback still work — you just won't get the live transcript, word count, or filler stats.
- Speech recognition language is set to English (`en-US`).

## Data & privacy

Transcripts, stats, and your session log are stored only in your browser's `localStorage`. Audio recordings exist only in memory for the current session (for playback) and are not saved to disk or persisted across page reloads — save the parts you want to keep before closing the tab.

Nothing is sent to a server for the core tool, because there is no server.

## Tech

Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS. Web Speech API for live transcription, MediaRecorder API for audio capture, Web Audio API for the soft timer chimes. Fonts are Playfair Display and Outfit, loaded from Google Fonts.

## License

MIT — use it, fork it, adapt the prompt banks to whatever you're practicing for.
